{
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "# Section 8 - Operate with OpenQASM",
                "",
                "- Task 8.1: Export circuits to OpenQASM 3",
                "- Task 8.2: Read OpenQASM 3 syntax and semantics",
                "- Task 8.3: Interoperate between QuantumCircuit and OpenQASM 3",
                "- Task 8.4: Understand Runtime REST API basics"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "Official references used:",
                "- https://openqasm.com/",
                "- https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/qiskit/qasm3/__init__.py",
                "- https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/test/python/qasm3/test_import.py",
                "- https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/apidocs"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "from io import StringIO",
                "from textwrap import dedent",
                "",
                "import requests",
                "from qiskit import QuantumCircuit",
                "import qiskit.qasm3 as qasm3"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "## Task 8.1 - Export circuits to OpenQASM 3"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "The core export API is `qiskit.qasm3.dumps(circuit)` for strings and `qiskit.qasm3.dump(circuit, stream)` for file-like objects.",
                "",
                "- `include \"stdgates.inc\";` is typically emitted for standard gates",
                "- exporter options such as `includes`, `basis_gates`, and `indent` are passed through keyword arguments"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "qc_export = QuantumCircuit(2, 2)",
                "qc_export.h(0)",
                "qc_export.cx(0, 1)",
                "qc_export.measure([0, 1], [0, 1])",
                "",
                "qasm_text = qasm3.dumps(qc_export)",
                "print(qasm_text)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "buffer = StringIO()",
                "qasm3.dump(",
                "    qc_export,",
                "    buffer,",
                "    includes=[\"stdgates.inc\"],",
                "    basis_gates=[\"U\"],",
                "    indent=\"    \",",
                ")",
                "",
                "print(buffer.getvalue())"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "## Task 8.2 - Read OpenQASM 3 syntax and semantics"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "For the exam, distinguish syntax from semantics:",
                "",
                "- OpenQASM 3 adds typed classical data such as `bit`, `int`, `uint`, `float`, and `angle`",
                "- measurement maps quantum data into classical storage",
                "- control flow such as `if`, `while`, and custom `gate` declarations changes program meaning, not just formatting"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "program = dedent(\"\"\"",
                "OPENQASM 3.0;",
                "include \"stdgates.inc\";",
                "",
                "input float[64] theta;",
                "qubit[2] q;",
                "bit[2] mid;",
                "",
                "gate bell_pair a, b {",
                "  h a;",
                "  cx a, b;",
                "}",
                "",
                "bell_pair q[0], q[1];",
                "mid[0] = measure q[0];",
                "if (mid[0] == 1) {",
                "  rz(theta) q[1];",
                "}",
                "mid[1] = measure q[1];",
                "\"\"\")",
                "",
                "print(program)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "## Task 8.3 - Interoperate between QuantumCircuit and OpenQASM 3"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "Interop is exam-relevant because export and import support are not symmetric.",
                "",
                "- `qasm3.dumps` and `qasm3.dump` are part of core Qiskit export",
                "- `qasm3.loads` and `qasm3.load` can require the optional `qiskit[qasm3-import]` extra",
                "- `loads_experimental` exists for the native experimental importer, but it supports a smaller feature set"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "roundtrip_source = qasm3.dumps(qc_export)",
                "",
                "try:",
                "    roundtrip_circuit = qasm3.loads(roundtrip_source)",
                "    print(\"Round-trip qubits:\", roundtrip_circuit.num_qubits)",
                "    print(\"Round-trip clbits:\", roundtrip_circuit.num_clbits)",
                "except Exception as exc:",
                "    print(\"Import requires qasm3 import support and feature compatibility:\")",
                "    print(type(exc).__name__, exc)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "unsupported_features = [",
                "    \"annotations or advanced constructs may need annotation handlers\",",
                "    \"unsupported grammar can raise QASM3ImporterError\",",
                "    \"round-trip fidelity depends on the features both sides understand\",",
                "]",
                "",
                "for item in unsupported_features:",
                "    print(\"-\", item)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "## Task 8.4 - Understand Runtime REST API basics"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "Section 8 also expects basic REST reasoning for Runtime workflows:",
                "",
                "- `POST` commonly creates a job resource",
                "- authentication is typically `Authorization: Bearer <token>`",
                "- polling uses job status until a terminal state such as `DONE`, `CANCELLED`, or `ERROR`",
                "- cancellation is usually modeled as `POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/cancel`"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "base_url = \"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api\"",
                "headers = {",
                "    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <token>\",",
                "    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",",
                "}",
                "payload = {",
                "    \"program_id\": \"sampler\",",
                "    \"backend\": \"ibm_brisbane\",",
                "    \"params\": {\"shots\": 4096},",
                "}",
                "",
                "submit_request = requests.Request(",
                "    \"POST\",",
                "    f\"{base_url}/v1/jobs\",",
                "    headers=headers,",
                "    json=payload,",
                ").prepare()",
                "",
                "status_request = requests.Request(",
                "    \"GET\",",
                "    f\"{base_url}/v1/jobs/<job-id>\",",
                "    headers=headers,",
                ").prepare()",
                "",
                "cancel_request = requests.Request(",
                "    \"POST\",",
                "    f\"{base_url}/v1/jobs/<job-id>/cancel\",",
                "    headers=headers,",
                ").prepare()",
                "",
                "for prepared in (submit_request, status_request, cancel_request):",
                "    print(prepared.method, prepared.url)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "python"
            },
            "source": [
                "terminal_states = {\"DONE\", \"CANCELLED\", \"ERROR\"}",
                "sample_statuses = [\"QUEUED\", \"RUNNING\", \"DONE\"]",
                "",
                "for status in sample_statuses:",
                "    print(status, \"terminal?\", status in terminal_states)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
                "language": "markdown"
            },
            "source": [
                "## Quick exam checklist",
                "",
                "- Use `qiskit.qasm3.dumps` and `dump` for export questions.",
                "- Remember that OpenQASM 3 adds typed classical data and control-flow semantics.",
                "- Treat `loads` and `load` as import APIs that can depend on optional importer support.",
                "- Expect REST questions about `POST`, bearer auth, versioned paths, polling, and cancellation endpoints."
            ]
        }
    ]
}
